{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1511822-play-with-umbral-and-physical-reflexion","id":1511822,"title":"Play with umbral and physical reflexion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-16T14:27:09-07:00","id":1511822,"title":"Play with umbral and physical reflexion","content":"Sometime it's hard to define how much physical world and penumbra can affect each other. I remember an exemple in the book saying that if a tree is cut in physical world it's umbral reflexion can survive for a long time but the opposite necessarly implies the death of the tree.<br /> How long will the physical entity survive after the death/destruction of it's counterpart? Hours? Days? Weeks?<br /> How about the case where you fights a bane in the penumbra, how will the claws mark and destruction manifest? A hole in a door after a gun shot for exemple, will the door in physical world degrade until it show the gun shot or just become fragile and visibly degraded?<br /> <br /> I've seen an old piece of art where we can see a werewolf fighting what it seems to be a serious disease spirit (bane?) while the patient is lying on a hospital bed. It made me wonder if a werewolf can fight an illness by interacting with it's spiritual counterpart (maybe with a ritual)?<br /> <br /> How have you treated with those interactions in your own story as ST?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","user":"Cain Loup-Noir","date":". 05-16-2023, 05:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T05:32:55-07:00","id":1511860,"title":"","content":"Umbra doesn't work by rules. It works by narrative and emotional relevance. Most buildings would have vague outlines and mostly undefined inner spaces,expect for the pattern webs fixing around what the outlines would be.<br /> <br /> So there tends to be much less to destroy in the umbra than in the real world, as less things reflect. This applies to other things as well, not every tree has a spirit, nor is everything in the world caused by spirits. A disease bane could be killing someone from the umbra by touching them from the outside and slowly rotting them from within, but usually it will just be a disease. Cold. Impersonal and without something to rip and tear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T06:03:24-07:00","id":1511864,"title":"","content":"Basically it's better to just make it work as i need instead of gathering details that can be different from an ST to another","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T06:59:25-07:00","id":1511867,"title":"","content":"Yup. Pretty much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T18:16:54-07:00","id":1511945,"title":"","content":"I was not really looking for rules but more some advice to use as ST, especially with that piece of art about a garou fighting the disease of his human friend in the umbra. It gives me tons of ideas for staging but I need enough detail to integrate this kind of event.<br /> <br /> I suspected that not EVERYTHING was reflected in the penumbra but I thought that playing with the rite of spirit awakening would allow a garou without mother's touch to save a human from his cancer or send a tool to a pack mate in a lab without taking the risk to be trapped in the gauntlet or precisely destroying an penumbral reflexion (let's say a security system panel) without direct interaction in the pysical world\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-17T20:19:06-07:00","id":1511962,"title":"","content":"Rite of spirit awakening would require you to interact with what you seek to awaken. How do you imagine it working on a part of someone's body?<br /> <br /> And just because you have a spirit of an item, doesn't mean you have an item. Even then, how much the spirit can interact with the real world depends on its power (unlikely to be high for a freshly awakened spirit) and the gauntlet (bound to be very high in any kind of a lab.<br /> <br /> You could bargain with the weaver spirits to turn things on and off for you (you can attack them too, but I would not recommend it), but don't expect things to exist in both worlds. The kind of security door that would exist in the umbra is the entrance to a theatere or maybe a 100 year old vault door that has been there since the opening of a bank, made as a unique masterpiece about who whole books were written and whose maker was a meticulous craftsman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T05:58:43-07:00","id":1512004,"title":"","content":"Hmm... let's imagine that:<br /> A kinflok has been put in jail by some shenanigans of a Pentex executive. You, as a garou, want to use the penumbra to enter the prison, join the kinfolk and then get him out with the help of spirits (thank to a chiminage or a gift/fetish to command them). If i understand you point, depending on how olf and/or important the prison is there might be no cells door, no alarm system or even no prison at all in the penumbra (wich make me wonder what happen if you cross the gauntlet from the penumbre in a place where there's a wall, will you be fused in the wall or just incapable to cross the gauntlet in that place?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-18T07:17:04-07:00","id":1512008,"title":"","content":"Why would the pentex executive even bother? Heck, why would you even contort your story into that? Kin are ordinary humans with human problems, which means they may end up incarcerated for a great many reasons. Not every problem in the world is of the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> Your plan is incredibly vague. What spirit? How can it affect the other side? This makes a world of difference because many spirits cannot affect or are even aware of the real world beyond &quot;it's there, I guess&quot;.<br /> <br /> The prison itself will depend. How old is it? How are the conditions in it? It could be a dehumanized clockwork machine run by Weaver spirits in a institution where absolute order invokes absolute compliance. It could be a horrifying pit of banes where attrocities committed by guards and inmates cover the walls with blood and pain, and where each new one emboldens the banes and inspires them to even more influence on the other side. Or it could just be a cold, dreary place where few spirits beside those of longing and sorrow would wish to consider. That's without getting into ghosts of course.<br /> <br /> All of that defines the umbral prison way more than what it looks like than the floorplans in the real world. The older it is and the stronger the emotions of the people in it the more solid those reflections will be - a solitary cell inhabitted by a man who has been there for ten years or the entry gate that everyone longs for to finally exit will be more real than most of the prison. it's going to have roughly the same layout, but some walls will be translucent and walkable, places where there are corridors may be covered in weaver webbing. Weaver webbing will be covering most buildings in an urban environment giving them a form beyond the building form. How sturdy and complex those are will depend on the nature of the place.<br /> <br /> It's best to compare umbra and real world as seeing a place and seeing it's map. They represent the same thing but in drastically different ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-19T16:30:35-07:00","id":1512157,"title":"","content":"Have you an exemple then of the way you would represent a place in physical world, it's umbral counterpart and how one could affect the other immediatly or with time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}